  abstract = {Initially envisaged as a guidance tool aimed at fostering the development of Chinese universities, the Shanghai Ranking has leapfrogged Chinese borders to become a barometer for the prestige of leading universities across the globe. A study of the last decade reveals the increasing success of Chinese universities in the ranking and confirms the country as a leading center of scientific achievement. In addition, by abridging the title of this global league table to the short form ``Shanghai Ranking,'' the media have contributed to raising the profile of a city and enhancing the framing power of an entire country, well beyond the academic sphere. The distribution of this ranking and its take-up by higher education leaders in numerous countries make it a formidable tool for leveraging China's diplomatic influence. Once described as the ``world's factory,'' China seeks to position itself as a powerhouse of the knowledge economy.},
