., (1994) The state and higher education, , London, London,: Woburn Press; Scott, P., (1995) The meaning of mass higher education, , Buckingham, UK, Buckingham,: Open University Press; Sennett, R., (2008) The craftsman, , London, London,: Allen Lane; Shattock, M., (1994) The UGC and the management of British universities, , London, London,: SRHE & Open University Press; Shore, C., Wright, S., Coercive accountability: The rise of audit culture in higher education (2000) Audit cultures: Anthropological studies in accountability, ethics and the academy, pp. 57-89. , In: Strathern M., editors London, London,: Routledge; Sinclair, A., The chameleon of accountability: Forms and discourses (1995) Accounting, Organisations and Society, 20 (2-3), pp. 219-237. , doi:10.1016/0361-3682(93)E0003-Y; Taggart, G.J., A critical review of the role of the English funding body for higher education in the relationship between the state and higher education in the period 1945-2003 (Unpublished PhD thesis, University of Bristol) (2004); Thompson, D.F., Moral responsibility of public officials: The problem of many hands (1980) American Political Science Review, 74 (4), pp. 905-916. , doi:10.2307/1954312; Trow, M., Trust, markets and accountability in higher education: A comparative perspective (1996) Higher Education Policy, 9 (4), pp. 309-324. , doi:10.1016/S0952-8733(96)00029-3; Wilson, L., (1979) American academics: Then and now, , New York, New York,: Oxford University Press},
