  abstract = {As the task of selecting an appropriate textbook for a course is difficult this article presents a procedure (checklist) which instructors might adopt to assist in their decision making. The Textbook Selection Checklist is developed from a strong empirical base and has been trialled to assess the relative merits of introductory and educational psychology textbooks published since 1975. The results of this assessment are provided and the implications for students, Instructors, and publishers are discussed. \copyright{} 1989, Taylor \& Francis Group, LLC. All rights reserved.},
