chool? Social and academic correlates of educational continuation after college (2003) Sociology of Education, 76 (2), pp. 143-169. , doi:10.2307/3090274; (1997) Higher education in the learning society, , http://www.leeds.ac.uk/educol/ncihe/, NCIHE, Retrieved November 2, 2010, from; (2010) Broke and broken: Taught postgraduate students on funding and finance, , http://www.nus-connect.org/news/article/postgraduate/942/, NUS, Retrieved November 15, 2011, from; Palmer, N., Bexley, E., James, R., (2011) Selection and participation in higher education: University selection in support of student success and diversity of participation, , http://www.go8.edu.au/university-staff/go8-policy-_and_-analysis/2011/selection-and-participation-in-higher-education, Retrieved May 1, 2011, from; (2009) Unleashing aspiration: The final report of the Panel on Fair Access to the Professions, , www.cabinetoffice.gov.uk/media/227102/fair-access.pdf, Panel on Fair Access to the Professions, Retrieved May 25, 2010, from; Park, C., Wells, P., (2010) The Higher Education Academy Postgraduate Taught Experience Survey (PTES) 2010 report, , http://www.heacademy.ac.uk/ourwork/supportingresearch/postgraduate/ptes, Retrieved October 22, 2010, from; Ross, J., Research expansion needs a research agenda (2010) Campus Review, , http://www.campusreview.com.au/pages/section/article.php?s=News&idArticle=15556, 19.4.10. Retrieved May 26, 2010, from; (2010) One step beyond: Making the most of postgraduate education, , www.bis.gov.uk/one-step-beyond, Smith Report, Retrieved November 15, 2010, from; Stuart, M., Lido, C., Morgan, S., Solomon, L., Akroyd, K., (2008) Widening participation to postgraduate study: Decisions, deterrents and creating success, , York, UK, York, UK,: Higher Education Academy; Thomas, L., Storan, J., Wylie, V., Berzins, K., Harley, P., Linley, R., Rawson, A., (2010) Analysis of widening participation strategic assessments 2009, , Ormskirk, UK, Ormskirk, UK,: Action on Access; Tobbell, J., O'Donnell, V., Zammit, M., Exploring transition to postgraduate study: Shifting identities in interaction with communities, practice and participation (2010) British Educational Research Journal, 36 (2), pp. 261-278. , doi:10.1080/01411920902836360; (2009) Promoting the UK doctorate: Challenges and opportunities, , UUK, Research report. London: Author; Wakeling, P., (2003) Social class and progression to postgraduate study in England, , Unpublished MA dissertation, University of York; Wakeling, P., La noblesse d'etat anglasie? Social class and progression to postgraduate study (2005) British Journal of Sociology of Education, 26 (4), pp. 505-522. , doi:10.1080/01425690500200020; Wakeling, P., (2009) A comparison of comparatively little, , June, Paper presented at the 2nd International RESUP Conference, Lausanne, Switzerland; Wakeling, P., Are ethnic minorities underrepresented in UK postgraduate study? (2009) Higher Education Quarterly, 63 (1), pp. 86-111. , doi:10.1111/j.1468-2273.2008.00413.x; Wakeling, P., (2009) Social class and access to postgraduate education in the UK: A sociological analysis, , Unpublished PhD thesis. University of Manchester; Wakeling, P., Kyriacou, C., (2010) Widening participation from undergraduate to postgraduate research degrees, , Swindon, UK, Swindon, UK,: NCCPE and ESRC; Waters, J.L., In pursuit of scarcity: Transnational students, 'employability' and the MBA (2009) Environment and Planning A, 41 (8), pp. 1865-1883. , doi:10.1068/a40319; Zimdars, A., Testing the spill-over hypothesis: Meritocracy in enrolment in postgraduate education (2007) Higher Education, 54 (1), pp. 1-19. , doi:10.1007/s10734-006-9043-3},
  abstract = {Widening participation is on the political agenda but, to date, policy, practice and research has focused on undergraduate education. This article identifies an emerging widening participation focus on doctoral education. Using England as a case study, the article examines this development within the context of the long-standing concern with equity in education, before reviewing the relatively small literature addressing who participates (and why) in doctoral and more general postgraduate education. An analysis of Widening Participation Strategic Assessments produced in 2009 by 129 English Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) reveals an emergent institutional awareness of this new development. Finally, a research agenda for widening participation to research degrees, focusing on research students, HEIs and policy-makers, is outlined. The conclusion calls for this agenda to be pursued at institutional, national and cross-national levels so that future policy can be made and implemented on the basis of a robust evidence base. \copyright{} 2013 Copyright HERDSA.},
