  issn = {07294360 (ISSN)},
  doi = {10.1080/0729436900090202},
  abstract = {The success of a tertiary level course, and of the students in it. formed the basis for this study. The focus is a longitudinal study of the 1973 entry cohort to the architecture course at the Western Australian Institute of Technology. Alternative approaches to ``success'' are defined. Inherent problems in reducing life-complexity to a limited number of variables are acknowledged. Something of the diversity of experiences and values of graduates and non-graduates is indicated. Finally, pluralism and lack of certainty in the post-modern world are commented upon. Reference is made to the potential for development of appropriate values, in the education process, against which each individual may. gauge his or her success. \copyright{} 1990, Taylor \& Francis Group, LLC. All rights reserved.},
