  abstract = {Summary Information for a follow-up study was successfully obtained from approximately one-half of the 1958 to 1966 applicants for American Cancer Society postdoctoral fellowships and the 1960 to 1966 applicants for faculty research awards. Recipients of either American Cancer Society grants or equivalent grants from other granting agencies had a more successful career than nonrecipients using level of academic appointment and number of publications as criteria. A relatively larger proportion of post-doctoral fellows than of those not funded remained in research activities.}
