her Education, 27 (4), pp. 369-386. , doi:10.1080/0307507022000011507; Kiley, M., Wisker, G., (2008) Now you see it, now you don't': Identifying and supporting the achievement of doctoral work which embraces threshold concepts and crosses conceptual thresholds, , June, June, Paper presented at third Threshold Concepts Conference, Kingston, ON; Kiley, M., Wisker, G., Threshold concepts in research education and evidence of threshold crossing (2009) Higher Education Research Development, 28 (4), pp. 431-441. , doi:10.1080/07294360903067930; Kiley, M., Wisker, G., Learning to be a researcher: The concepts and crossings (2010) Threshold concepts: Theory to practice, , In: Meyer J. H.F., Land R., editors Amsterdam, Amsterdam,: Sense; Lee, A., Green, B., Supervision as metaphor (2009) Studies in Higher Education, 34 (6), pp. 615-630. , doi:10.1080/03075070802597168; Lee, A., How are doctoral students supervised? Concepts of doctoral research supervision (2008) Studies in Higher Education, 33 (3), pp. 267-281. , doi:10.1080/03075070802049202; Manathunga, C., Goozée, J., Challenging the dual assumption of the 'always/already' autonomous student and effective supervisor (2007) Teaching in Higher Education, 12 (3), pp. 309-322. , doi:10.1080/13562510701278658; Maslow, A.H., A theory of human motivation (1943) Psychological Review, 50 (4), pp. 370-396. , doi:10.1037/h0054346; McAlpine, L., Jazvac-Martek, M., Hopwood, N., Doctoral student experience: Activities and difficulties influencing identity development (2009) International Journal for Researcher Development, 1 (1), pp. 97-112. , doi:10.1108/1759751X201100007; McAlpine, L., Paulson, J., (2010) Untold doctoral stories: Cultural narratives of neglect, , December, December, Paper presented at the Society for Research into Higher Education conference, Newport, Wales; Meyer, J.H.F., Land, R., (2003) Threshold concepts and troublesome knowledge: Linkages to ways of thinking and practising within disciplines, , Occasional Report No. 4. Swindon, UK: TLRP/ESRC; Meyer, J.H.F., Land, R., Threshold concepts and troublesome knowledge. 2: Epistemological considerations and a conceptual framework for teaching and learning (2005) Higher Education, 49 (3), p. 373. , doi:10.1007/s10734-004-6779-5; Meyer, J.H.F., Land, R., (2006) Overcoming barriers to student understanding: Threshold concepts and troublesome knowledge, , In: Meyer J. H.F., Land R, editors Abingdon, UK, Abingdon, UK,: Routledge; Morris, C., Wisker, G., (2011) ESCalate interim report, , York, UK, York, UK,: Higher Education Academy; Morris, C., Wisker, G., Cheng, M., Lilly, J., Warnes, M., Robinson, G., Trafford, V., (2010) Well-being and the research student, , Falmer, UK, Falmer, UK,: University of Brighton Press; Muurlink, O., Poyatos Matas, C., A higher degree of stress: Academic well-being (2010) Well-being and the research student, pp. 60-71. , In: Morris C., editors Falmer, UK, Falmer, UK,: University of Brighton Press; Nightingale, P., (2005) Advising PhD candidates, , Milperra, NSW, Milperra, NSW,: HERDSA; Pargetter, R., Transition: From a school perspective (2000) Journal of Institutional Research, 9 (1), pp. 14-21; Poyatos Matas, C., (2008) An innovative approach to research supervision, , July, July, Paper presented at the University of Brighton Learning and Teaching Conference, Brighton, UK; Poyatos Matas, C., A new approach to research supervision (2009) Social purpose and creativity: Integrating learning in the real world, , In: Barlow J., Louw G., Price M., editors Falmer, UK, Falmer, UK,: University of Brighton Press; Poyatos Matas, C., Tannoch-Bland, J., The academic life balancing skills program: A window into academic well-being for research students International Journal of Doctoral Studies, , (under review); Ryff, C., Keyes, C., The structure of psychological wellbeing revisited (1995) Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 69 (4), pp. 719-727. , doi:10.1037/0022-3514.69.4.719; Shacham, M., Od-Cohen, Y., Rethinking PhD learning incorporating communities of practice (2009) Innovations in Education and Teaching International, 46 (3), pp. 279-292. , doi:10.1080/14703290903069019; Watson, D., Schuller, T., (2009) Learning through life: Inquiry into the future for lifelong learning, , Leicester: NIACE; Wisker, G., (2005) The good supervisor, , Basingstoke, UK, Basingstoke, UK,: Palgrave Macmillan; Wisker, G., (2010) Nudging': Exploring effective strategies to enable postgraduate research students to cross conceptual thresholds in their doctoral work, , July, July, Paper presented at the Third Threshold Concepts Symposium, Sydney, Australia; Wisker, G., Morris, C., Cheng, M., Masika, R., Warnes, M., Lilly, J., (2010) Doctoral learning journeys: Final report, , York, UK, York,: Higher Education Academy; Wisker, G., Robinson, G., Kiley, M., Crossing liminal spaces: encouraging postgraduate students to cross conceptual thresholds and achieve threshold concepts in their research (2008) Quality in postgraduate research: Research education in the new global environment. Part 2: Conference proceedings, , In: Kiley M., Mullins G., editors Canberra, Australia, Canberra, Australia,: CEDAM, ANU; Wisker, G., Robinson, G., Trafford, V., Warnes, M., Creighton, E., From supervisory dialogues to successful PhDs: Strategies supporting and enabling the learning conversations of staff and students at postgraduate level (2003) Teaching in Higher Education, 8 (3), pp. 383-397. , doi:10.1080/13562510309400; Wisker, G., Savin-Baden, M., Priceless conceptual thresholds: Beyond the 'stuck place' in writing (2009) London Research Education, 7 (3), pp. 235-247. , doi:10.1080/14748460903290207},
  abstract = {Much research into doctoral student-supervisor relations focuses on developing positive interactions. For many students, however, the research experience can be troubled by breakdowns in communication and even the loss of the supervisor(s), turning the student into a doctoral 'orphan' and impacting on their academic identity and ability and confidence in producing a sound doctoral-level contribution to knowledge. Our work with a range of UK- and internationally-based doctoral students looks specifically at reasons for supervisor loss and/or absence and the students' experience of being doctoral 'orphans' in terms of identity, confidence and progress. In focusing on those who achieve successful completion, it suggests the need for institutional and community support and highlights the development of effective strategies leading to ownership, empowerment and emotional resilience. \copyright{} 2013 Copyright HERDSA.},
  langid = {english},
  keywords = {academic identity,completion,doctoral students,postgraduate,supervisors}
}

